<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Hugo Bootstrap Theme</title><link>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/</link><description>Recent content on Hugo Bootstrap Theme</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><copyright>Open-source &lt;a class="text-muted text-decoration-none" href="https://github.com/filipecarneiro/hugo-bootstrap-theme/blob/main/LICENSE"&gt;MIT&lt;/a&gt; Licensed.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:03:23 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Structured Data Demo 🔎</title><link>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/page/structured-data-demo/</link><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/page/structured-data-demo/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="structured-data-demo"&gt;Structured Data Demo&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This page exists to exercise the page-level JSON-LD partials that ship with the
theme, so their output is validated on every build rather than only when a real
site happens to configure them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three schemas are emitted from the front matter above:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://schema.org/Product" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Product&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — via &lt;code&gt;product:&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://schema.org/SoftwareApplication" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;SoftwareApplication&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — via &lt;code&gt;softwareApplication:&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://schema.org/FAQPage" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;FAQPage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — via &lt;code&gt;faq:&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The site-level schemas (&lt;code&gt;WebSite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Organization&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;LocalBusiness&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Event&lt;/code&gt;)
are configured in &lt;code&gt;config/_default/params.toml&lt;/code&gt; and render on the home page.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Hugo v0.119.0</title><link>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/hugo-v0-119/</link><pubDate>Sun, 24 Sep 2023 00:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/hugo-v0-119/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/hugo-v0-119/hugo-logo.svg" alt="Hugo" width="1493" height="391" fetchpriority="high" class="img-fluid mb-5"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This version is built with Go 1.21.1 which contains some relevant security fixes for the html/template package, see &lt;a href="https://github.com/golang/go/issues/62196" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Issue 62196&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://github.com/golang/go/issues/62197" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Issue 62197&lt;/a&gt;. This is the main reason Hugo 0.119.0 is released sooner rather than later. But this release also comes with a dependency refresh and some useful image processing improvements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A new general-purpose &lt;a href="https://gohugo.io/content-management/image-processing/#process" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Process&lt;/a&gt; method and filter.
A new &lt;a href="https://gohugo.io/functions/images/#opacity" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Opacity&lt;/a&gt; filter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/gohugoio/hugo/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Release Notes on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Bootstrap 5.3.0</title><link>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/</link><pubDate>Tue, 30 May 2023 00:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/bootstrap-5-3_hu_fbe9445fa6788212.webp" alt="Bootstrap 5 3" srcset="https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/bootstrap-5-3_hu_17bcd2a4dcdb1343.webp 480w, https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/bootstrap-5-3_hu_42536b176bc2a357.webp 768w, https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/bootstrap-5-3_hu_54c07882800c8a1d.webp 1024w, https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/post/bootstrap-5-3-0/bootstrap-5-3_hu_fbe9445fa6788212.webp 1432w" sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 1140px, 100vw" width="1432" height="777" fetchpriority="high" class="img-fluid"&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s official, the final stable release of v5.3.0 has landed! It’s been a monumental effort to revamp our codebase for CSS variables and color modes, one that will see continued changes leading up to an eventual Bootstrap 6. And we’re so excited to finally ship it!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On top of all the work that’s gone into this release, a lot has happened behind the scenes since we shipped our pre-releases. Keep reading to learn everything that’s &lt;a href="https://blog.getbootstrap.com/2023/05/30/bootstrap-5-3-0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;new in v5.3.0&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Bootstrap Carousel 🎠</title><link>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/page/bootstrap-carousel/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jun 2022 00:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://filipecarneiro.github.io/hugo-bootstrap-theme/page/bootstrap-carousel/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="bootstrap-carousel"&gt;Bootstrap Carousel&lt;/h1&gt;
